;; The conversion of the test tool checked by a round trip through fexpr:
;; each example X.fl of the directory above, and of ../ocaml, is converted to
;; a term of the Rocq model, that term is printed back as fexpr, read again
;; by the compiler's parser and converted again, and the two terms of the
;; model are compared (see ../../tools/flroundtrip.ml).
;;
;; Nothing is to be added here for a new example: its round trip is expected
;; to be the same. An example that the conversion refuses says why itself,
;; and passes. Any other answer ("round trip DIFFERS", "not printable", "not
;; read back", "names not read back"), and an answer that is missing, fails
;; until what the tool prints is recorded here, in
;; X.expected for ../X.fl and in ocaml_X.expected for ../ocaml/X.fl, with
;; the reason: `dune promote` writes the file, and the reason goes in
;; README.md.
;;
;; The rules are generated by gen_rules.sh from the files that are there, and
;; are included by run/dune, as for the directory above.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files ../*.fl)
  (glob_files ../ocaml/*.fl)
  (glob_files *.expected))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc
   (run sh %{dep:gen_rules.sh} %{deps}))))
